<title>CROATIA: Croatian Dec oil, natural gas output rise slightly.</title>
<headline>Croatian Dec oil, natural gas output rise slightly.</headline>
<dateline>ZAGREB 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The State Statistics Bureau issued the following oil and natural gas output details.</p>
<p> CROATIA OIL EXTRACTION     DEC '96    NOV '96     DEC '95</p>
<p> Crude oil (tonnes)	   129,445    128,700     125,317</p>
<p> Natural gas (000 cu m)     157,984    155,316     168,880</p>
<p>PETROLEUM PRODUCTS (tonnes)</p>
<p> Gasoline			  89,216    121,492     105,214</p>
<p> Gas oil			   81,593     94,541	74,405</p>
<p> Heating oil		    167,352    212,864     168,640</p>
<p>Data exludes production from oilfields in Serb-held Eastern Slavonia which was partly restarted in August 1995.</p>
<p>-- Zagreb Newsroom, 385-1-4557075</p>
</text>
